Ulrich Eckhardt wrote:
>
> I'm currently wondering why enhancing skills is not done automatically. Are
> there any options that I might gain from not #enhancing a skill as soon as
> I can?

There are 30 possible skill slots once you have reached XP 30, and
once you've used up a skill slot with #enhance you can never get it
back by choice.

Advancing from Unskilled to Basic costs 1, from Basic to Skilled
costs 2, from Skilled to Expert costs 3.  For ANY ONE skill class.
So going from Unskilled to Expert costs 1+2+3 = 6 experience
levels.

Several classes have more possible skill classes enabled than can
ever be acheieved by level 30 because of the above cost.  Especially
since getting an artifact gift opens that skill slot to Basic even
if your character class started restricted in it.

There are many skill classes whose weapons are poor and more skill
classes that have no artifact weapons.  Without Mjollnir it is an
utter waste to #enhance the crappy war hammer.  Flails may never
be worth advancing.  Advance to Expert in Dart, run out of darts,
and you have commited a colossal waste.

Weapon skills are very much a limited resource and strategy should
be applied to putting them to good use.  If your character gets
Greyswandir but can't have the skill slot to get it to Basic,
that would be a shame.

So many characters *can* become at least Basic in both Dagger and
Knife.  But daggers are far better weapons than knives and there
are several artifact daggers and no artifact knives.  Only a
cryknife user will ever want to advance Knife rather than Dagger.

The weapons used by an early character tend to be different from
those used by a middle character tend to be different from those
used by an ascension-kitted character.  The skills involved must
be taken into account.

For a Valkyrie the strategy can be simple - Advance dagger and
long sword to Expert as soon as possible and silver saber and
war hammer to Basic or Skilled as soon as possible ignoring other
weapon classes if needed.  Then spend the rest of your skills
whereever seems appropriate based on what's in your cache.
For other character classes that strategy is poor and picking
the optimal one is much more of a trade-off.

